CASE: AWPTCM-T33366  (206) Authentication&Security_WebAuthentication - Promiscuous / Intercept web Authentication
  ck.db: status Draft, STEP_BY_STEP, num_steps 1 with an EMPTY step, has_objective 0. Nothing authored beyond the title.

What the title means on THIS build (read before drafting steps):
  - qmark `auth-web-server ?` (13:30 NZDT): dhcp, host-name, intercept-port, ip-conflict-prefer-newer-supplicant,
    ipaddress, login-url, page, ping-poll, port, redirect-delay-time, redirect-url, session-keep, ssl, trustpoint.
    `auth-web-server mode ?` -> % Unrecognized command. There is NO `mode {intercept|promiscuous}` and NO
    `auth-web-server gateway` on this build.
  - AW+ Technical Tips and Tricks (docs.atlnz.lc, tips-and-tricks_aw-_revd.pdf p.73, p.78) describes older
    `auth-web-server mode 'intercept' and 'promiscuous'`, where the switch captures ARP, DNS and HTTP from the
    supplicant to send it the login page, and fakes the supplicant's gateway.
  - Command Reference 5.5.6-1 `auth-web-server intercept-port` (published): "If this command is not specified,
    AlliedWare Plus Web-Authentication intercepts the supplicant's initial TCP port 80 connection to a web page
    and sends it the Web-Authentication Login page"; `intercept-port <1-65535>|any` adds ports, `any` = all TCP.
  So intercept is built in (port 80, to ANY destination) and extendable; that is what is tested. The ARP-capture
  half ("promiscuous") is not configurable here and `auth forward arp` (auto-added) forwards ARP anyway.

Steps (derived from the title):
  S1 an UNAUTHENTICATED client's HTTP to an OFF-SUBNET address (8.8.8.8, routed via the DUT) gets the DUT's login page;
     the answer on the wire comes from the DUT's MAC. Control: TCP 8080 and 8081 are NOT intercepted.
  S3 `auth-web-server intercept-port 8080` -> 8080 intercepted; control 8081 still not.
  S4 `auth-web-server intercept-port any` -> 8081 intercepted too.
  S5 after web login, nothing is intercepted: the same requests are ROUTED by the DUT.
Expected: S1/S3/S4 login page (form posting to http://192.168.50.1/index.cgi) answered by e0:1a:ea:d5:04:56; controls
  time out with SYNs unanswered; S5 no login page.

Host change (D2 + Test Engineer 13:3x "Yes, add the narrow helper"): tb5 route 8.8.8.0/24 via 192.168.50.1 dev eth6,
  added and removed with tools/hostnet.py (commit 9b9287b) via `tools/tb sudotool tb5 auth1304 hostnet ...`.
  jm1-jm5 NOT used (eth6 itself is the client; it has no session at the start of this case).

